.TH LO 5N UniSoft
.SH NAME
loop \- software loopback interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
pseudo-device loop
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I loop\^
interface is a software loopback mechanism which may be
used for performance analysis, software testing, and/or local
communication.  The interface is Internet addressable as network
127 (decimal).  The local host is host 1.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP .3i
\fBlo%d: can't handle af%d\fP
The interface was handed
a message with addresses formatted in an unsuitable address
family; the packet was dropped.
.SH SEE ALSO
inet(5N), net(5N).
.SH BUGS
It should handle all address and protocol families.
.\"N	 @(#)lo.5N	 5.2 of 7/12/84
